        "text": "Hardware wallets are physical electronic devices that use a random number generator to generate public and private keys. The keys are then stored in the device itself, which isn't connected to the Internet. As such, hardware storage constitutes a type of cold wallet and is deemed as one of the most secure wallets, but they require some expertise and are less user friendly. You should consider using a hardware wallet if you plan to hold your crypto for a long time, or if you're holding large amounts of crypto.",
